<p>A rule's premise can combine conditions with AND, OR, “at least <i>n</i> of”, NOT, thresholds on 0–10 scales, age,
  sex, concepts, scores and beliefs. Here is rule D-PE-1 as the engine prints it from the graph:</p>
<pre>IF   Wells score for pulmonary embolism &gt; 4
AND  (pleuritic chest pain OR shortness of breath OR coughing up blood)
THEN pulmonary embolism (CF +0.70)
<span class="c">source: Wells et al. (2000) · fidelity: partial (heart rate and “PE most likely” cannot be asked)</span></pre>
<p>Rules fire in <span class="g">strata</span>: a rule runs only after the rules that produce the concepts and scores it
  reads, which is exactly the relay order above. When the rule base is loaded it is validated: every reference must
  exist, the strata must be consistent, and there must be no cycles.</p>
</section>

